<IndustryPage {...pageData}>
<p>UK agriculture is navigating a period of unprecedented change - new subsidy schemes, tightening environmental requirements, and the pressure to produce more with less. The farms thriving in this environment are the ones using data to make better decisions about inputs, yields, and compliance. Yet many UK farms still rely on paper records, spreadsheets, and disconnected apps that make it impossible to see the whole operation in one place.</p>
<p>Off-the-shelf agricultural software rarely matches how UK farms actually work. Generic farm management packages force you to adapt your field naming, your livestock grouping, and your spraying workflow to their structure. They can't handle the specific compliance requirements of your assurance scheme, the way you batch your livestock movements, or the equipment service intervals specific to your machinery fleet. Compliance tools generate reports in their format, not the format your inspector wants. The result is farmers maintaining shadow spreadsheets because the official system can't capture the realities of their operation.</p>
<p>We build custom software for UK farms and agricultural businesses that fits your exact operation. From livestock tracking and crop management to supply chain and equipment maintenance, we build systems that work the way you work. We understand UK agriculture - from the field to the farm office - and we build software that records the right data automatically and generates compliance reports without the scramble. Whether it's a bespoke livestock tracker that handles ear tags, medications, and movement notifications, or a crop management system that links spray records to field boundaries and yield data, bespoke software fits your farm.</p>
<p>Agricultural compliance carries real consequences. Red Tractor assurance, DEFRA movement regulations, cross-compliance rules, and RPA subsidy claims all demand meticulous record-keeping. A missed spray record or an unrecorded livestock movement isn't just a paperwork gap - it's a potential subsidy penalty or assurance suspension. Bespoke software records pesticide use, fertiliser applications, and livestock movements as they happen, with automated alerts for medication withdrawal periods and movement notifications - replacing paper-based systems that are easily lost and impossible to search during an inspection.</p>
<p>A UK mixed farm with 400 head of cattle and 800 acres of arable was struggling to produce accurate Red Tractor compliance records during annual inspections. Their paper-based system meant days of preparation and occasional gaps that put their assurance at risk. We built a bespoke farm management system with a mobile app for field and livestock recording, automated compliance report generation, and equipment maintenance tracking. Inspection preparation dropped from three days to two hours, medication withdrawal alerts eliminated a near-miss on a calf sold too soon after treatment, and the farm identified £12,000 in unrecovered equipment maintenance costs within the first year.</p>
<p>Agriculture is a sector where bespoke software delivers clear value. Every field, every animal, and every input generates data. The opportunity is building software that turns that data into better decisions, automated compliance, and a clear picture of your whole operation - from the field to the farm gate.</p>

